    "status": "confirmed",
    "reasoning": "For q-38546, both one-sided limits at x=-1 equal -1, whereas f(-1)=1. Neither one-sided continuity condition holds, so statements I, II, and III are false. For q-73105, the left-hand limit at x=3 is 3, whereas f(3)=1 and the right-hand limit is 1. Thus only right-continuity holds, making statement II alone true. Both answers agree with the earlier response and each question's captured worked solution. No grade evidence was supplied.",
